The 4000-500 uses DSSI to access disks and if it were my system I'd
stuck to that.
Since used/refurbished DSSI disks are probably too difficult or too
expensive I'd try a
DSSI-to-SCSI converter and put that in a BA cabinet. An HSD05 or an
HSD10 would be my choice.
That way you can use fairly cheap SCSI-2 disks.
ISTR that the KZQSA has some limitations, so I'd stay away from it.
Never met a KZCCA so can't help you there.
An LPV11 supports the LP11 parallel lineprinters, the LP11 and LGnn
models sold by DEC.
Perhaps you could connect it to a parallel to serial converter and use
an LA75 on it!
Hans


