There are two kinds of parallel interface for printers: the big
computer world uses Dataproducts, and the PC world has Centronics. LPV
=3D Dataproducts. Converters are possible, involving e.g. inverting a
handful of status bits (can't remember the exact details). Maybe
commercial converters were available, not sure, but it seems unlikely
(albeit not impossible) now.

Making a CXY08 cable for your LA120 sounds more appealing, if all you
want is a printer of some kind. But you don't get the quite the same
end result as with a proper drum or chain or even line-matrix (eg LG
series) printer. Maybe that's good.


