Phillip, it is really rather simple to open an SBB brick.
- remove the four screws located in the bottom
  =3D> these screws hold the disk in place
- push a flat screwdriver into the recesses near the front bezel,
first one side then the other
  =3D> the front comes off; it remains attached to the brick owing to a
flat cable that holds it
- use a slightly larger screwdriver and push it ito the slightle
larger recesses (front and rear on each side)
  =3D> The top comes off and the rear connector is now free to move as
well
- lift the drive out of the shelf
  =3D> blue boxes tend to hold SCA (80 pin SCSI) drives and the
connector comes off really easy.

The SCA disks are simple, no jumpers to set, everything is set via the
80 pin plug.
Put the connector on the target drive and repeat the previous steps in
reverse order.
Really, nothing to it
Hans


