The catalogue is from the DEC 3000 era, before the Jensen/DECpc AXP150/
DEC2000 and long before the PWS. I do remember that by the time the
PWS came out, DEC prices for NT-only Alpha boxeswere actually not a
million miles off the prices for the equivalent x86 DEC box (for a
while, there were equivalent Alpha and x86 boxes). Making a PWS/NT VMS-
ready or Tru64-ready added a bit, but maybe not as much as some people
remember, and at that time the VMS/UNIX boxes were reasonably
competitive with other vendors' UNIX boxes. But it was too late, PCs
were on the way to world domination, whether or not they made sense in
any given business.


