I recently acquired a TZ30 tape drive. It does not want to load any tapes I 
put in it. The odd thing is that when I insert a tape it does not get held 
in place, I have to hold it in place while I move the lock lever across. I 
am not sure if this is normal as I have never used a TZ30 before.

While I am holding the tape in place the green light comes on and does not 
flash. After moving the lever to the lock position the lights flash a few 
moments and then the green light flashes to tell me there is a problem with 
the tape. However the drive mechanism makes no attempt to load the tape (I 
can see this because I have the cover of the system removed, there is no 
movement in the drive mechanism). I have opened up the drive and the tapes 
leader looks fine.

Does anyone know of any well-known faults that might cause the tape to fail 
to load?

I am also slightly puzzled though about how the drive works. I can see what 
look like some motors to drive the capstans, but I cannot see a motor which 
drives the spool, so I don't understand how it can pull tape out of the 
cartridge.

Thanks

Rob




