Hello.
As far as I know, there's no capstan inside. There are only two motors
for tape movements, one connected to the cassette spool,
one to the spool inside the drive.
When you insert a cassette and move the lock lever, the mechanism
should open the cassette door, while the tape leader holder will
put it in the right position. The tape-leader end, made like a sort of
hook, will attach to the hole at the end of the tape inside
the cassette. At this time the empty spool of the drive begins to
rotate, taking the tape out of the cassette spool.
You could try to do this operation manually with the drive turned off,
dismounting the cover of the drive.
If all is ok and the tape-leader is not broken, you could try to clean
the optical and electromechanical sensors that the drive
uses to understand if the tape is correctly hooked to the tape-leader
and if the cassette is correctly inserted.
Let me know if you need some help.
Andrea


