Previously, it was usual to put 8in floppies on PDP-11s.

As I understand it, the RQDX1 is supposed to work with the RX50,
which is a single side 80 track drive (and disk).

Such drives exist, but are not common on PCs.

The usual PC/AT style HD/DD drive runs at 360RPM, too fast.
You might be able to use the speed adjustment and get it
down to 300RPM.

The PC style 3.5in drive runs at 300RPM, so should work.

-- glen


