But is it an 80 track (per side) drive?  If not, it will run
into the stop near track 40 very fast.
 
> So I asked nicely how to bootstrap with that thing.

Do you have the drive select jumper set right?
Some number 0 to 3, others 1 to 4.  Most will turn on the motor
without drive select, but some have an option for that.

There are some funny difference between drives, that otherwise
follow the standard.  Mostly those are on line 2 and line 34,
which aren't quite standard.  Pin 34 might be "door open", and if
the drive doesn't give the right signal, the controller might
wait until you close the door.
 
