Just a silly question: Do you have the right cable and is it connected
correctly? Unlike PCs, there should be no twisty bits in the cable,
nor is the cable itself twisted between the box and the drive (not on
a DEC drive anyway). The test is that every other pin is earth, so on
one side of the connector every pin is connected together.

IIRC even an incompatible drive will do various clicks and clunks on
reset, and can often even be read, though you may not get all the
blocks.

Have you tried all the sockets on the backplane connector? I have a
vague recollection that only one works with the floppy (or that each
has a different unit number).

Chris


