I forgot about this till the recent DECnet discussion jarred it from
my memory. Thought it might be useful to some ppl.
Linux has had DECnet phase IV as part of its kernel since early 2.3x
releases.
It supports LAT, but not LAD/LAST.
I used it a few times perhaps 3 years ago...seemed to work fine when I
used it exercising some x-windows apps.

Unfortunately, in 2/18/2010 it has been orphaned....see:
http://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v2.6/ChangeLog-2.6.33

You can read about it here...http://sourceforge.net/apps/mediawiki/
linux-decnet/index.php?title=Main_Page

John



