> I wonder what a 'llogin -d -v' shows for these RSX-11 systems?

It will show the service just fine. And you can connect to the RSX 
system with llogin as well (don't people actually read what I write?).

The problem is that after a while, your RSX system will crash. (Note how 
I said "after a while".)

Looking at the system before that, you can observe the LAT unknown frame 
counter increase. You might also experience lost connections, which will 
force you to do a new connect, as the Linux LAT and RSX LAT gets out of 
sync.

I would suspect that the VMS LAT also will notice the bad frames, but 
that it handles it more gracefully than RSX do.
(Yes, it is obviously a bug in the RSX LAT implementation that 
unrecognized frames cause a memory leak that eventually crash the 
system. Anyone give me the source to the RSX LAT, and I'll happily fix 
it. Until then, the best hope would be to fix the protocol violation in 
the Linux LAT code, which is available.)

	Johnny

