As far as I can tell from the announcement this is a case of Chrissie
moving away from the DEC arena, no longer interested in being the
DECnet for Linux maintainer and the project being orphaned because no-
one is willing to take over. A similar situation has arisen in the
continued development of various UNIX variants on Alpha platforms, I
believe Gentoo is the only official distribution of Linux now with
continued support for Alpha. Time and again it appears to be
developers no longer being interested in the platform, or
alternatively, feeling like they are wasting their time because of the
limited take-up. To a certain extent this is equally true of
alternative operating systems for HP IA64 platforms.

I do use DECnet for Linux, and will be sad to see it disappear in
future (as it will make my life more difficult) but I can't argue with
there not being an active maintainer.

$0.02 as always. Mark.


